WEBVTT

00:00:01.252 --> 00:00:05.464
Ima kara utau koto koko dake no hanashi ni

00:00:06.924 --> 00:00:08.926
<i>Shite oite ne</i>

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:14.724
<i>Yokubou wa kokoro ni
kakushite okitai no hontou wa</i>

00:00:14.807 --> 00:00:16.851
<i>Himitsu himitsu</i>

00:00:33.117 --> 00:00:35.703
<i>Chikamichi shitai</i>

00:00:35.786 --> 00:00:39.582
<i>Ame ni nureru koto naku</i>

00:00:39.665 --> 00:00:43.211
Kaze ni tobasareru koto naku

00:00:43.294 --> 00:00:47.006
Zurugashikokute mo waratte ne

00:00:47.089 --> 00:00:51.469
<i>Hikyoumono demo asonde ne</i>

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:55.056
Kanashimitakunai

00:00:55.139 --> 00:00:58.935
Namida ni nureru koto naku

00:00:59.018 --> 00:01:02.563
<i>Tohou ni kureru koto</i> naku

00:01:02.647 --> 00:01:06.025
Donkan datte waratte ne

00:01:06.108 --> 00:01:11.072
<i>Tanoshii koto dake oshiete ne</i>

00:01:14.825 --> 00:01:19.372
<i>Mitai kao ga aru no kikitai koe ga aru no</i>

00:01:20.581 --> 00:01:24.252
Me <i>ga</i> sametara yorokobi wo narashite

00:01:24.335 --> 00:01:30.299
<i>Ohayou, kyou mo yoroshiku onegai itashimasu</i>

00:01:30.299 --> 00:01:30.967
"Princess Jellyfish"

00:01:36.222 --> 00:01:38.266
Okay, next! I'm cranking them out today!

00:01:38.349 --> 00:01:41.519
What's your name, again? You, the one
who always blends into the background!

00:01:42.436 --> 00:01:44.814
Y-You mean me?

00:01:44.897 --> 00:01:46.399
Right! Put this on!

00:01:46.482 --> 00:01:47.692
And this, too!

00:01:47.775 --> 00:01:48.734
Er...

00:01:51.779 --> 00:01:53.823
It's plenty dry already...

00:01:53.906 --> 00:01:56.325
These things aren't just for drying hair!

00:01:56.409 --> 00:01:58.369
Tsukimi! Go take a bath, right now!

00:01:58.452 --> 00:02:00.746
Y-You're doing me, too?

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:02.748
We're all going to dress up!

00:02:02.832 --> 00:02:06.419
I'll show you people a
dramatic before-and-after!

00:02:12.591 --> 00:02:15.886
Sorry to call you all the way out here.

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:18.889
Thank you so much. This was a big help.

00:02:18.973 --> 00:02:20.516
Thank you for returning it so quickly.

00:02:20.599 --> 00:02:23.436
Say, are you free?

00:02:25.104 --> 00:02:28.274
Let me buy you a drink,
as my thanks for the umbrella.

00:02:28.649 --> 00:02:31.569
"Night of the Living Sisterhood"

00:02:35.156 --> 00:02:39.660
Might I ask why I'm the
only one dressed as usual?

00:02:39.744 --> 00:02:45.207
Oh, you're fine just the way you are!
It's just a question of framing.

00:02:45.291 --> 00:02:47.376
F-Framing?

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:50.588
Okay, it's time for Clara's Style Check!

00:02:50.671 --> 00:02:54.050
Here's Chieko surrounded
by the "Before" Sisterhood.

00:02:54.133 --> 00:02:56.969
Surrounded by a panther, a Three
Kingdoms geek, an Afro-wearing train geek,

00:02:57.053 --> 00:02:59.305
and Tsukimi the jellyfish geek,

00:02:59.388 --> 00:03:02.266
you can tell at a glance that
she's a traditional-dress geek!

00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:03.893
But... ta-dah!

00:03:03.976 --> 00:03:05.770
Can you believe it, ladies and gentlemen?!

00:03:05.853 --> 00:03:08.356
With Tsukimi and the others looking all Stylish,

00:03:08.439 --> 00:03:13.694
she instantly becomes a celebrity
who wears a kimono because she's rich!

00:03:13.778 --> 00:03:17.365
And that's all for today's Style Check Corner!

00:03:17.448 --> 00:03:21.243
See? So your "before" is your "after."

00:03:21.327 --> 00:03:25.998
I-| see! I don't know whether
to feel pleased or left behind...

00:03:26.082 --> 00:03:29.293
Don't worry, next time I'll give
you a big transformation too.

00:03:29.377 --> 00:03:32.254
L-| wasn't fishing for one.

00:03:32.338 --> 00:03:36.467
Okay, then. Shall we all go
out for an after-dark teatime?

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:39.678
--But we have plenty of
dokudami tea right here--

00:03:39.678 --> 00:03:41.055
--Don't be silly! --But we have
plenty of dokudami tea right here--

00:03:41.055 --> 00:03:45.976
"Amamizu-kan"

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:48.104
C-Café?!

00:03:48.187 --> 00:03:53.359
Coming in at #1 on this week's
"Words to Make the Sisterhood's Hearts Stop":

00:03:53.359 --> 00:03:54.610
"Number 1 "

00:03:54.693 --> 00:03:56.987
"Café"

00:04:00.157 --> 00:04:01.534
Mayaya!

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:05.788
Villain! What did you put in my shoes?!

00:04:05.871 --> 00:04:08.916
Nothing. Don't get your blood up;
they're just spike heels.

00:04:08.999 --> 00:04:11.877
What?! You spiked the heels
with bloodsucking leeches?!

00:04:11.961 --> 00:04:12.753
I knew they felt wobbly!

00:04:12.837 --> 00:04:16.507
Like hell I did! Your ankle wobbled!

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:18.467
I'm going to change into normal shoes.

00:04:18.551 --> 00:04:20.261
Me too.

00:04:20.344 --> 00:04:21.470
No Way!

00:04:21.554 --> 00:04:24.390
No woman is properly
armed without her high heels!

00:04:24.473 --> 00:04:27.059
People say "Style starts from the feet up," right?

00:04:27.143 --> 00:04:30.855
They might hurt a little, but you
have to start getting used to them.

00:04:30.938 --> 00:04:34.233
If you let the enemy see you
trip during battle, you'll look lame!

00:04:34.316 --> 00:04:38.028
Um, you keep using words
like "enemy" and "battle"...

00:04:38.112 --> 00:04:40.781
What exactly are you planning?

00:04:40.865 --> 00:04:44.660
Like I said, I'm planning to stop
them from tearing down Amamizu-kan!

00:04:44.743 --> 00:04:47.788
"Stop them"? How?

00:04:47.872 --> 00:04:50.040
What will you do to stop them?

00:04:53.252 --> 00:04:56.088
I haven't thought that part through yet!

00:04:56.172 --> 00:04:57.673
So you have no plan!

00:04:57.756 --> 00:05:02.136
You insolent Wench! Disembowel
yourself in apology to Kong Ming!

00:05:02.219 --> 00:05:05.973
It'll be fine. If we all brainstorm together,

00:05:06.056 --> 00:05:08.684
we'll hit on a good strategy soon enough.

00:05:08.767 --> 00:05:10.561
Today we're preparing for that moment

00:05:10.644 --> 00:05:14.815
by doing training exercises in...
transformation? Cosplay? Yeah!

00:05:14.899 --> 00:05:18.903
You just pulled that out of
your rear end, didn't you, Meat?

00:05:18.986 --> 00:05:22.907
A speech so winged would stun even
LU Bu! This cannot be easily forgiven!

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:26.744
Shut up, you! And Mama
didn't name her boy "Meat," either!

00:05:26.827 --> 00:05:27.953
"Boy"?

00:05:28.037 --> 00:05:32.041
<i>P</i> Olé! Come on now, everybody, let's go! <i>P</i>

00:05:32.124 --> 00:05:33.000
"P Five of us going with one of... <i>P</i>

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.211
--Right, then! Just shut up and come on!
"P Five of us going with one of... <i>P</i>

00:05:35.294 --> 00:05:38.881
And if you fall down, you
get right back up, you got that?!

00:05:43.719 --> 00:05:46.514
I think "redevelopment" is
a reexamination of the role

00:05:46.597 --> 00:05:48.849
that we want certain land to play.

00:05:48.933 --> 00:05:53.229
Though that's just my
personal opinion, of course.

00:05:53.312 --> 00:05:56.273
I'll admit that many of the
features I'd like to see in a city

00:05:56.357 --> 00:05:58.734
are inadequate in the Amamizu Station area.

00:05:58.817 --> 00:06:03.614
Exactly. There's almost no luxury space.

00:06:05.366 --> 00:06:06.951
Excuse me for a moment.

00:06:08.285 --> 00:06:10.287
Go right ahead.

00:06:10.371 --> 00:06:12.039
Hello, Father.

00:06:12.122 --> 00:06:15.626
Yes, I'm speaking with
that developer we discussed.

00:06:15.709 --> 00:06:18.504
Yes. I believe if we can gather information...

00:06:21.549 --> 00:06:23.008
My apologies.

00:06:23.092 --> 00:06:24.260
No need.

00:06:31.809 --> 00:06:34.687
Do you hold your drink well, Mr. Koibuchi?

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:37.731
As well as the next man, I suppose...

00:06:37.815 --> 00:06:39.567
But with your position to think of,

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:42.278
I imagine you don't let yourself get drunk.

00:06:42.361 --> 00:06:44.113
After all, you're "Koibuchi Junior,"

00:06:44.196 --> 00:06:47.032
the man whose political debut
is fast approaching, aren't you?

00:06:47.116 --> 00:06:50.828
Oh, no, I'm still just my father's Hunky.

00:06:50.911 --> 00:06:55.583
And second-generation Diet members
aren't regarded well these days, either.

00:06:55.666 --> 00:07:00.588
Also, the factions within ruling
party are all fallin' outta step...

00:07:00.671 --> 00:07:04.842
So I gotta shay... right now
the pollickle shfere'ss a Iil...

00:07:04.925 --> 00:07:10.264
Huh? Polli... Iickti... cal...

00:07:10.347 --> 00:07:12.933
Are you all right? Shall we go somewhere else?

00:07:22.276 --> 00:07:27.865
Wow. The Buddhas of Bamiyan?
No, more like Bamboo Hat Jizos!

00:07:27.948 --> 00:07:30.326
Come on, girls, relax.

00:07:32.119 --> 00:07:33.412
Not happening, eh?

00:07:33.495 --> 00:07:36.707
What'll you have to drink?
Order whatever you want!

00:07:36.790 --> 00:07:38.917
Oh, I guess that's not happening either, huh?

00:07:39.001 --> 00:07:41.295
They've got cocktails here, too!

00:07:41.378 --> 00:07:43.589
Yeah, not happening.

00:07:43.672 --> 00:07:47.468
It's okay, you know. Look up there!

00:07:50.137 --> 00:07:52.556
You all look great.

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:54.683
You don't look out of place at all.

00:07:54.767 --> 00:07:56.977
So stop freaking out.

00:07:57.061 --> 00:08:00.230
You can just act like you're
drinking tea at Amamizu-kan.

00:08:02.566 --> 00:08:05.152
But there's no dokudami tea here!

00:08:05.235 --> 00:08:07.029
Mayaya's sensitive to the cold,

00:08:07.112 --> 00:08:09.948
so she can't sleep if she doesn't
have some dokudami tea before bed.

00:08:10.032 --> 00:08:13.410
I've been getting awful chills lately, too...

00:08:13.494 --> 00:08:14.953
Excuse me!

00:08:15.037 --> 00:08:16.288
<i>Yes'?</i>

00:08:16.372 --> 00:08:18.540
Do you have drinks that
would warm someone up?

00:08:18.624 --> 00:08:21.877
Yes, milk tea with ginger is a good choice,

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:24.296
or we also have various sweet hot cocktails.

00:08:24.380 --> 00:08:28.926
Feh! Listen to her and her "milk tea"!
It's just hot ginger water!

00:08:29.009 --> 00:08:33.305
That just gives me goose
bumps. A-And it's 800 yen?!

00:08:33.389 --> 00:08:34.973
They're trying to rip us off.

00:08:35.057 --> 00:08:40.312
Okay, bring us some of that milk tea.
A sampling of the hot cocktails, too.

00:08:40.396 --> 00:08:44.149
<i>L-I'll</i> have this green tea cocktail.

00:08:44.233 --> 00:08:48.654
This looks delicious!
The caramel pa... "parfait"?

00:08:48.737 --> 00:08:51.240
It looks like a par-fay in the picture.

00:08:51.323 --> 00:08:53.117
You'll find out if you order it.

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:54.993
But it's so expensive.

00:08:55.744 --> 00:08:57.538
I've got the money!

00:08:57.621 --> 00:09:00.791
The whole night's on me, so you
girls order all the food you want!

00:09:00.791 --> 00:09:00.916
"Because I'm the son of a rich man!"

00:09:02.918 --> 00:09:06.422
--Meat! Meat! Meat! --Caramel parfait! --One clubhouse
sandwich and one pasta with prawns in tomato cream sauce!

00:09:06.505 --> 00:09:08.424
Who is this "Bagna Céuda" person?!

00:09:08.507 --> 00:09:09.883
Come on, Tsukimi, you too.

00:09:10.801 --> 00:09:15.389
Okay... I'll have one of these
"Margherita" pizzas, please.

00:09:20.352 --> 00:09:25.107
Oh, dear. Maybe that drug
was a little too effective on you.

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:27.317
What a cute sleeping face.

00:09:27.401 --> 00:09:30.612
I think <i>I'll</i> make it my wallpaper.

00:09:30.696 --> 00:09:32.281
Pardon me!

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:39.913
Cheese.

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:43.292
Ugh, this lighting is terrible!

00:09:43.375 --> 00:09:47.463
There's a shadow right over
my laugh lines! Delete! Delete!

00:09:47.546 --> 00:09:51.550
I'll kill the overhead light...
use just this one... okay!

00:09:51.633 --> 00:09:55.929
Ack, no! Now it's too dark!
Switch to nighttime mode!

00:09:56.013 --> 00:09:58.348
Gotta hold my breath and keep my hand still.

00:09:58.432 --> 00:10:03.896
No, don't move! You just sleep.
Sleep like the dead kings of ancient Egypt!

00:10:03.979 --> 00:10:05.981
Yes, there's a good boy.

00:10:06.064 --> 00:10:08.442
Now then, <i>I'll</i> just dig in.

00:10:14.615 --> 00:10:17.242
Time to dig in!

00:10:17.326 --> 00:10:18.035
--Ah, it tastes like a par-fay!

00:10:18.035 --> 00:10:19.536
--Tasty raw meat!
--Ah, it tastes like a par-fay!

00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:20.496
You mean uncooked ham.

00:10:20.579 --> 00:10:22.956
Th-There are grains in the bread!

00:10:26.877 --> 00:10:31.173
Oh, I love this! It's so sweet!

00:10:31.256 --> 00:10:33.717
<i>Th-That's cute...!</i>

00:10:33.801 --> 00:10:35.677
<i>She's blowing on her drink!</i>

00:10:35.761 --> 00:10:40.307
Bagna! Bagna, Bagna, Bagna!

00:10:40.390 --> 00:10:42.017
I can see the Kaiji limited express!

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:46.480
Aha, the Chuo Line.
Now I know where we are!

00:10:46.563 --> 00:10:49.942
Excuse me, would you mind if we
switched to a table on the terrace?

00:10:55.614 --> 00:10:57.407
It's beautiful...

00:10:59.910 --> 00:11:02.079
Look, a Mitsu-501!

00:11:04.248 --> 00:11:06.291
This view!

00:11:06.375 --> 00:11:10.754
I see before me the burning capital
of Luoyang, set ablaze by Dong Zhuo!

00:11:18.971 --> 00:11:23.851
Yep, they love it!
Looks like they've finally relax...

00:11:27.855 --> 00:11:32.025
The moon tonight looks
just like a moon jelly...

00:11:35.362 --> 00:11:38.532
It's almost like we're underwater!

00:11:42.661 --> 00:11:45.163
Th-That was freakin' <i>cute!</i>

00:11:45.247 --> 00:11:48.667
<i>You</i> can't <i>gaze dreamily into the
night sky with your eyes all sparkly</i>

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:51.503
<i>and say it looks like we're underwater!</i>

00:11:51.587 --> 00:11:53.171
<i>That's cheating, dammit!</i>

00:11:53.255 --> 00:11:55.716
Hey, what are you doing?!
Quit pounding on the stall!

00:11:55.799 --> 00:11:57.175
Please excuse me!

00:11:58.343 --> 00:12:00.304
Burn it all to the ground!

00:12:16.528 --> 00:12:19.698
Well, good morning.

00:12:21.241 --> 00:12:22.284
It's commercial time!

00:12:22.367 --> 00:12:23.327
Clara!

00:12:24.661 --> 00:12:25.829
It's the second half!

00:12:25.913 --> 00:12:26.705
Tequila!

00:12:40.218 --> 00:12:42.179
You trashed, honey?

00:12:50.562 --> 00:12:52.022
Want a drink?

00:12:54.066 --> 00:12:55.776
Is mineral water all right?

00:12:55.859 --> 00:12:59.488
Please let me have my clothes.

00:12:59.571 --> 00:13:01.281
Is the fizzy kind all right?

00:13:01.365 --> 00:13:03.408
It used to be too much for me,

00:13:03.492 --> 00:13:06.286
but since my trip to
Italy I've learned to drink it.

00:13:06.370 --> 00:13:08.246
Please let me have my clothes.

00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:14.086
Look! This is a photo of the trip to
Paris I took with my old friend Yoko!

00:13:14.169 --> 00:13:16.755
Where are my clothes?

00:13:16.838 --> 00:13:21.134
Tokyo is a city with as many
stars as its people have dreams,

00:13:21.218 --> 00:13:25.597
and as much neon light as its
people have despair, don't you think?

00:13:29.267 --> 00:13:31.728
Goodness, going home already?

00:13:31.812 --> 00:13:34.982
I apologize for giving you
so much trouble. Good night.

00:13:36.441 --> 00:13:40.028
Wait, now, you forgot your pants.

00:13:40.112 --> 00:13:42.698
Honestly, you're so absentminded.

00:13:44.032 --> 00:13:46.159
That was really good.

00:13:46.243 --> 00:13:48.829
It seems we've got great chemistry.

00:13:56.795 --> 00:14:00.340
My head just smacked against the floor...
who treats a woman this way?!

00:14:00.424 --> 00:14:02.843
--It was very gracious of you to
buy a sandwich for Ms. Mejiro too!

00:14:02.843 --> 00:14:05.012
--VVow, an aerial view of the Kaljl! --It was very
gracious of you to buy a sandwich for Ms. Mejiro too!

00:14:05.095 --> 00:14:07.014
--It's nothing.
--That was fun...

00:14:07.097 --> 00:14:09.307
Luoyang Fire!

00:14:09.391 --> 00:14:12.394
Hey Meat, buy me that raw
meat again sometime, okay?

00:14:12.477 --> 00:14:16.064
That was uncooked ham!
And don't call me "Meat"!

00:14:17.774 --> 00:14:21.695
I have a perfectly good name,
and it's "Kuranosuke," so--

00:14:21.778 --> 00:14:22.738
" Kura"?

00:14:22.821 --> 00:14:28.285
U-Uh... K-Kura... Kurako?

00:14:28.368 --> 00:14:30.954
<i>That's the most unreal-sounding name ever!</i>

00:14:33.540 --> 00:14:35.917
--Kurakko! Kurakko! --What a wonderful
name! It sounds so old-world Japanese!

00:14:35.917 --> 00:14:37.753
--VVouldn't "KuHa"-ko be better? --What a
wonderful name! It sounds so old-world Japanese!

00:14:37.836 --> 00:14:39.629
<i>They</i> believed me!

00:14:41.048 --> 00:14:44.509
That's right, I'm Kurako! Right, Tsukimi?

00:14:44.593 --> 00:14:50.015
And you know what, Clara?
The moon looked like a moon jelly today!

00:14:50.098 --> 00:14:53.977
<i>O-Oh God, the barf-worthy
act of talking to a jellyfish</i>

00:14:54.061 --> 00:14:56.605
<i>is looking cute to me for some reason!</i>

00:14:56.688 --> 00:14:59.524
I ate so much my pants are too tight...

00:14:59.608 --> 00:15:00.609
My foot!

00:15:00.692 --> 00:15:01.902
Heh, I just walked home barefoot.

00:15:01.985 --> 00:15:03.820
Well, I'll be heading home now!

00:15:03.904 --> 00:15:05.363
Really?

00:15:05.447 --> 00:15:07.616
See you later, Kurako.

00:15:08.408 --> 00:15:11.995
<i>Ugh! Is it just me, or am
I really uncool right now?</i>

00:15:14.539 --> 00:15:16.666
Welcome home, Kura-pyon!

00:15:16.750 --> 00:15:19.753
Hi-dee-ho there, good nephew!

00:15:19.836 --> 00:15:22.380
Oh, Uncle Saburota,
I didn't know you were here.

00:15:22.464 --> 00:15:24.883
Don't you have too much
on your plate to be visiting us?

00:15:24.966 --> 00:15:27.094
I'm here because I've
got too much on my plate!

00:15:27.177 --> 00:15:31.181
Unless your papa saves my little
behind, I'll be in deep doo-doo!

00:15:31.264 --> 00:15:33.183
Huff, huff, huff!

00:15:33.266 --> 00:15:34.518
Kuranosuke!

00:15:34.601 --> 00:15:36.186
How many times do I have to tell you?

00:15:36.269 --> 00:15:38.897
Don't show your face in
front of me dressed like that!

00:15:38.980 --> 00:15:41.566
Rig ht, Fight, sorry!

00:15:57.249 --> 00:15:59.835
<i>Hakutsuru... maru!</i>

00:15:59.918 --> 00:16:03.296
Uncle, what are you doing?!
I'll take you to court!

00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:06.424
No, no, Kura-pyon, you've got it all wrong.

00:16:06.508 --> 00:16:09.803
I finished my private chat with
your papa, so now it's your turn.

00:16:09.886 --> 00:16:10.554
What?

00:16:10.595 --> 00:16:14.641
Someone told you about what
happened to Shu-Shu, didn't they?

00:16:14.724 --> 00:16:16.268
What "happened" to him?

00:16:16.351 --> 00:16:19.688
Hmm? But isn't that why
you called me the other day

00:16:19.771 --> 00:16:22.566
fishing for dirt about his
relationships with women?

00:16:22.649 --> 00:16:28.238
Nah, I just figured you
might know about his love life.

00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:32.284
Whoops, I'm about to miss Gaki no Tsukai.

00:16:32.367 --> 00:16:33.952
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait!

00:16:34.035 --> 00:16:37.956
What the heck?! Finish what you were saying!
You know you got me curious!

00:16:38.039 --> 00:16:41.835
Oh, Kura-pyon, you naughty boy!
No one will want me for a wife now!

00:16:41.918 --> 00:16:43.712
Get back here, Baldy!

00:16:46.590 --> 00:16:48.967
Damn! Where did he go?!

00:16:56.933 --> 00:16:58.810
B-Brother dearest?

00:16:58.894 --> 00:17:05.483
What's wrong? You look like some
soap opera heroine who just got molested...

00:17:05.567 --> 00:17:07.152
" Molested " ...?

00:17:08.486 --> 00:17:10.280
Crap! Baldy escaped!

00:17:12.199 --> 00:17:16.578
So that's it... I guess I was molested...

00:17:22.751 --> 00:17:25.128
Hanamori, bring the car around!

00:17:25.212 --> 00:17:26.296
Don't touch.

00:17:26.379 --> 00:17:30.884
Right, right, sorry. I see
you're waxing. Which means...

00:17:30.967 --> 00:17:33.345
I have to let it dry for another ten hours,

00:17:33.428 --> 00:17:35.472
so it's impossible for me to
take you anywhere right now.

00:17:35.555 --> 00:17:37.349
I can't believe this!

00:17:38.225 --> 00:17:41.478
Hello? Uncle Saburota?
Why did you run away?!

00:17:41.561 --> 00:17:45.690
Tell me what you were talking about!
I'm too curious to sleep!

00:17:45.774 --> 00:17:50.195
I tried to get Hanamori to go after
you in the car, you know! Seriously!

00:17:50.278 --> 00:17:53.448
Huh? Hanamori? Yeah, he's here.

00:17:57.077 --> 00:17:58.328
Hanamori.

00:17:58.411 --> 00:17:59.496
<i>Yes'?</i>

00:17:59.579 --> 00:18:03.708
Uncle said if I wanted to know why
Shu's got such a phobia of women,

00:18:03.792 --> 00:18:05.752
I should ask you.

00:18:09.005 --> 00:18:13.260
I think you're better off not knowing.

00:18:13.343 --> 00:18:15.303
No, I'm not!

00:18:17.472 --> 00:18:22.143
If you don't tell me, I'll plaster
my hands all over this shiny hood!

00:18:22.227 --> 00:18:24.854
--There's a reason for Shu's woman phobia.
--You didn't even last a second!

00:18:24.854 --> 00:18:26.982
--It all started 21 years ago, when he was
only nine. --You didn't even last a second!

00:18:27.065 --> 00:18:30.485
Your father took him to see a musical...

00:18:30.568 --> 00:18:34.322
...and he saw your father and Lina...

00:18:34.406 --> 00:18:35.991
...together.

00:18:45.041 --> 00:18:46.710
Hanamori?

00:18:46.793 --> 00:18:49.379
Could I ask you to bring the car around?

00:18:51.548 --> 00:18:54.134
It won't come off!

00:18:54.217 --> 00:18:57.929
No matter how many times I wash my
hair and my face, this stuff won't come off!

00:18:58.013 --> 00:19:01.725
Good grief... Maybe we're
out of soap and shampoo.

00:19:01.808 --> 00:19:04.853
Tsukimi, could you run to lwahashi
drug store and pick up some more?

00:19:04.936 --> 00:19:06.855
--I can't get it off!
--Roger!

00:19:06.938 --> 00:19:08.898
I'm on my way!

00:19:19.743 --> 00:19:23.913
I'm sorry to come so late, and looking like this.

00:19:23.997 --> 00:19:26.166
Could I ask you to shake my hand?

00:19:40.013 --> 00:19:41.389
Thank you.

00:19:44.184 --> 00:19:47.354
I apologize for disturbing you. Good night.

00:19:50.190 --> 00:19:53.151
Huh? Huh? Huh?!

00:19:55.862 --> 00:20:02.660
Shu, I'm afraid I told
Kuranosuke about your trauma.

00:20:02.744 --> 00:20:05.872
I'm sorry. I found myself in
an impossible predicament...

00:20:05.955 --> 00:20:08.917
O-Oh, I see. Right.

00:20:10.293 --> 00:20:14.422
Well, you've always been like that.

00:20:14.506 --> 00:20:16.091
I'm sorry.

00:20:18.343 --> 00:20:23.264
Father! Father, where did you go?

00:20:23.348 --> 00:20:27.894
We have to hurry back home.
Mother is waiting for us!

00:20:27.977 --> 00:20:30.480
She said to come home early,

00:20:30.563 --> 00:20:33.942
because we're having
sukiyaki for dinner. It's your favorite.

00:20:42.158 --> 00:20:43.743
Father...?

00:20:47.914 --> 00:20:51.626
That's some pretty heavy stuff.

00:20:51.709 --> 00:20:54.170
Right, we didn't do anything.

00:20:54.254 --> 00:20:57.549
But he thinks we did, one hundred percent.

00:20:57.632 --> 00:20:59.551
Yeah, it's no problem!

00:20:59.634 --> 00:21:00.885
Sure, I got pics.

00:21:00.969 --> 00:21:05.014
He was so flustered he left
something behind, so when I go return it,

00:21:05.098 --> 00:21:08.309
I'll use my rad moves to
wrap him around my little finger.

00:21:08.393 --> 00:21:11.312
What? You think my slang's out of date?

00:21:11.396 --> 00:21:16.317
The 80's?! Can it, or <i>I'll</i> knock you flat!

00:21:16.401 --> 00:21:18.570
Brother...?

00:21:20.738 --> 00:21:29.747
<i>Hontou ni kizuite hoshii n da,
anata ga utsukushii tte koto wo</i>

00:21:29.831 --> 00:21:34.169
Ima made naze kizukanai no sa

00:21:34.252 --> 00:21:38.673
<i>Kokoro nakushita mitai da yo</i>

00:21:38.756 --> 00:21:47.849
<i>Sugu ni sugu ni kizuite hoshii, wakatte hoshii yo</i>

00:21:47.932 --> 00:22:02.322
<i>Sugu ni kimi ni kizuite hoshii,
kimi no kirei ni kizuite hoshii yo</i>

00:22:03.698 --> 00:22:08.161
Anata <i>ga</i> totemo kirei dakara

00:22:08.244 --> 00:22:12.248
Anata ni sore wo tsutaetai no sa

00:22:12.332 --> 00:22:21.925
<i>ltsumademo, itsumademo kimi utsukushisa wo</i>

00:22:22.008 --> 00:22:30.391
Anata <i>ga</i> jibun no utsukushisa ni
kizuitara boku <i>wa</i> shiawase nan da

00:22:30.475 --> 00:22:35.146
<i>Boku wa kimi wo omotteru yo</i>

00:22:35.230 --> 00:22:44.489
<i>Kimi no kirei ni kizuite okure</i>
